# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the build context root, so a
# bare `scripts` excludes only the top-level one. `.gitignore` is NOT reused
# here -- the two files have different semantics, and this file is what decides
# what COPY can see.
.git
.github
.freebuff
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local state: runtime artifacts, datasets, network caches, HF cache, decks.
# These are large and must never be in the image.
data/
runs/
tests/
.cache/
hub/
*.pptx
*.log

# NOTE: `artifacts/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It is ~20 KB of committed
# benchmark evidence and the console's Evaluation tab reads it on startup, so a
# container with no run history still shows the measured numbers. Both
# Dockerfiles COPY it and assert it at build time.

# Docs and planning notes are not needed at runtime.
*.md
!requirements.txt

# `scripts/` is intentionally NOT ignored: the image ships the reproduction
# scripts (benchmark/calibration entry points), and an ignored directory cannot
# be COPYed -- that combination is what previously made `docker build` fail.

inputs.txt
LICENSE
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.demo
.dockerignore
.gitignore
